  "description": "TIJLIK crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C210 H196 Dy8 N24 O44 4+,4(Cl1 O4 1-),2(C1 H4 O1),12(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 11 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.585-4.160 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.67-123.85°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C212H228Cl4Dy8N24O74. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
